data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1** to **OpenAPI.NET v2**. This is a major breaking change in the underlying library. Here's what changed and how to fix each issue:

---

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` removed

The `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace and its types (`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc.) are gone. Examples are now raw `JsonNode`.

```csharp
// Before
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

---

## 2. `OpenApiResponse` → responses are keyed differently

`operation.Responses` is now of type `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` but the `Description` property is still there. This part likely still compiles — but if you're getting errors, ensure you're not using the old `OpenApiResponses` wrapper type explicitly.

---

## 3. `OpenApiReference` / `ReferenceType` changes

`ReferenceType` is now a **string-based** type (`ReferenceType` enum removed). Use the `OpenApiReference` constructor with a target ID:

```csharp
// Before
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// After
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme();
oAuthScheme.Ref = "oauth2";   // or use OpenApiReference with string target
```

Or using the new reference model:

```csharp
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2")
};
```

---

## 4. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI v3.1 (which v2 of the library targets) no longer uses `nullable`. Instead, `type` becomes an array that includes `"null"`.

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After — no-op for false; for setting nullable=true you'd do:
// property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type | JsonSchemaType.Null;

// To ensure NOT nullable, remove null from the type flags:
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

Note: `Schema.Type` is now a flags enum (`JsonSchemaType`) rather than a string.

---

## 5. `schema.Required` is now `ISet<string>` (unchanged) but `schema.Properties` values are `OpenApiSchema`

This part is mostly the same, but double-check your `using` directives — remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;` and add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;`.

---

## Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2")
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of breaking changes:**
| v1 (`.NET 9`) | v2 (`.NET 10`) |
|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger` | `JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` enum | `new OpenApiReference("id")` |
| `schema.Nullable = bool` | `schema.Type` flags with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
